,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OCCURRENCE: posting 'recheck-review' on Gerrit change 1577 CANCELLED the in-flight CI run.\n\nTimeline (change 1577, patch set 3):\n  02:14:40  rebar CI bot: Patch Set 3: -Verified  STARTED: .../actions/runs/31349238794\n  02:15:07  me: 'recheck-review' comment\n  02:15:32  rebar CI bot: Patch Set 3: Code-Review-1 Verified-1  CANCELLED: .../31349238794\n\nNet effect: the review was NOT retriggered (bug b0f5 — fire-and-forget queue) and a healthy CI\nrun was killed, leaving a Verified -1 that reflected the cancellation rather than any real\nfailure. Triaging that took a full cycle to attribute, because a cancellation and a genuine\nfailure present identically as Verified -1.","timestamp":1786377098096106001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR DECISION 2026-08-12: option (c) — rename our LLM retrigger word so it cannot collide with the external CI 'recheck' matcher (we do not own lfit/releng-gerrit_to_platform). Scope: pick a non-prefix-colliding trigger (e.g. 'rereview-llm' or similar), update retrigger.py matcher + docs + any templates; keep accepting the old word for a deprecation window if cheap.","timestamp":1786502571783340001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATOR CONFIRMED 2026-08-12: hard cutover — NO deprecation window (keeping the old word alive keeps the CI collision alive). The old 'recheck-review' word gets a clear refusal reply naming the new trigger word.","timestamp":1786503650096215001}],"created_at":1786227385213896001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4bd228ca-c4f7-4bd3-ae62-70a30c13c1e9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"deeb-89c1-1080-4690"},{"link_uuid":"0ab980c2-8228-4f6b-8f76-2a3859079e25","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e1aa-28c9-e9a2-45a6"}],"description":"## Context\n\nOur LLM re-review trigger word collides with the EXTERNAL CI ChatOps matcher we do not own\n(lfit/releng-gerrit_to_platform). `infra/gerrit/gerrit_to_platform.ini.template` maps\n`recheck = verify` under `[mapping \"comment-added\"]`, and g2p's comment matcher is\nsubstring-based, so a comment containing the retired LLM word (which embeds `recheck`)\nALSO dispatches the Verified workflow — cancelling an in-flight CI run and leaving a\n`Verified -1` that reflects a cancellation, not a failure (observed on changes 1551 and 1577).\n\nOur own matcher (`src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py`) is already whole-word safe; the\ncollision is entirely on the CI side, which we cannot change. OPERATOR DECISION (option c,\n2026-08-12): RENAME our trigger. HARD CUTOVER, no deprecation window — keeping the old word\nalive keeps the collision alive. The retired word gets a clear refusal reply naming the new\ntrigger.\n\nAdditional finding from triage: the bot's OWN reply texts (`_ACCEPTED_MESSAGE` and\n`_refusal_message`) currently embed the retired word verbatim. Those are posted as Gerrit\ncomments, so the bot's replies are themselves a live source of spurious CI dispatch. Any\ntext the bot posts must be scrubbed too, not just the matcher.\n\n## Design\n\nNew trigger token: **`rerun-llm-review`**.\n\nChosen because it contains no `[mapping \"comment-added\"]` key from the ini template as a\nsubstring (the only key is `recheck`), no ini key contains it, and it names both the\nmechanism (rerun) and the gate (llm-review) so it cannot be confused with CI's `recheck`.\nThe substring-safety property is pinned by a test that PARSES the ini template rather than\nhardcoding `recheck`, so adding a future CI ChatOps mapping that collides fails the suite.\n\nChanges:\n- `retrigger.py`: `TRIGGER_TOKEN = \"rerun-llm-review\"`, `_TOKEN_RE` matched on the new word\n  with the same `-`/`_`-binding word boundaries. Add `_RETIRED_TOKEN_RE` for the old word.\n- Handler order (each earlier check sees strictly less attacker-controlled input):\n  loop guard -> token match (new OR retired) -> project guard -> change-key check ->\n  `get_change_event` re-anchoring -> [retired? post refusal, return None] -> eligibility ->\n  reset. The retired branch is placed AFTER the project guard and AFTER re-anchoring because\n  `post_comment` needs the re-anchored `change_id`/`revision` and must never reply on an\n  out-of-project change; a retired-word comment on a non-matching project, a missing\n  change key, or an unresolvable change is a silent no-op like any other. The retired branch\n  NEVER enqueues a review and NEVER writes a label; it posts exactly one best-effort\n  `post_comment` refusal and returns `None`.\n- The retired-word refusal, the findings refusal, and the accepted reply must all be free of\n  every ini-mapped trigger word. The retired-word refusal therefore refers to the old trigger\n  descriptively (\"the former LLM re-review trigger word\") instead of spelling it, since\n  spelling it would re-dispatch CI from our own comment.\n- Every remaining retired-word occurrence outside the detector is updated to the new word:\n  `app.py:176` and `reconcile.py:25` descriptive comments; `docs/review-policy.md`,\n  `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/adr/0069-retryable-coverage-gap-bounded-deferral.md`,\n  `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`,\n  `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md`, `infra/gerrit/webhooks.config`. After the change the\n  retired word survives in `src/rebar/` in exactly ONE file — `retrigger.py` — where the\n  detector regex and the module docstring explain the cutover.\n- Tests: EVERY retired-word occurrence in `tests/unit/test_review_bot_retrigger.py`,\n  `tests/unit/test_review_bot_retrigger_attestation_6a81.py`, and\n  `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` moves to the new token — module docstrings, fixture\n  defaults (`_comment_event`), positive-form lists, the near-miss parametrize list (which\n  becomes `rerun-llm-reviews` / `pre-rerun-llm-review` / `rerun-llm-review-x`), forged\n  attacker/summary strings, and inline comments — with the SOLE exception of the new cases\n  that deliberately exercise the retired word's refusal branch. New cases added: the\n  retired-word refusal, and the ini-substring-safety assertions.\n\nOut of scope (explicitly): `infra/gerrit/gerrit_to_platform.ini.template`. The `recheck`\nmapping stays as-is; it is CI's word.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — A `rerun-llm-review` comment drives the existing accepted path (eligibility ->\n      fixed-neutral reset -> forced review event), and near-miss forms\n      (`rerun-llm-reviews`, `pre-rerun-llm-review`, `rerun-llm-review-x`) remain silent\n      no-ops.\n      Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot_retrigger.py -q`\n- [ ] AC2 — A comment carrying the retired word never returns a review event, never resets a\n      vote, and posts exactly one refusal reply that names `rerun-llm-review`.\n      Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"retrigger or recheck\"`\n- [ ] AC3 — No text the bot posts to Gerrit (accepted reply, findings refusal, retired-word\n      refusal) contains any `[mapping \"comment-added\"]` key parsed from\n      `infra/gerrit/gerrit_to_platform.ini.template`.\n      Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"retrigger or recheck\"`\n- [ ] AC4 — `TRIGGER_TOKEN` contains no ini-mapped comment-added trigger key as a substring,\n      and no ini key contains `TRIGGER_TOKEN`; the assertion reads the ini template at test\n      time rather than hardcoding the word.\n      Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"retrigger or recheck\"`\n- [ ] AC5 — Contributor-facing documentation instructs the new word only; no doc, guide, or\n      runbook still tells a contributor to comment the retired word.\n      Verify: `grep -rn \"recheck-review\" docs/ src/rebar/_guides/ AGENTS.md CONTRIBUTING.md infra/`\n      returns ZERO lines (the ADR is updated too, so there is no exempt residue).\n- [ ] AC5b — The retired word survives in `src/rebar/` in exactly one file, the detector's own\n      module (`retrigger.py`), never as an instruction elsewhere in the package.\n      Verify: `grep -rl \"recheck-review\" src/rebar/` outputs exactly the single line\n      `src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py`.\n- [ ] AC5c — The retired word survives under `tests/` only in the module that exercises its\n      refusal branch.\n      Verify: `grep -rl \"recheck-review\" tests/` outputs exactly the single line\n      `tests/unit/test_review_bot_retrigger.py`.\n- [ ] AC6 — Gates are green.\n      Verify: `make lint && make typecheck && python -m pytest tests/interfaces -q -k \"review_bot or retrigger\"`","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py","reason":"Rename TRIGGER_TOKEN/_TOKEN_RE to rerun-llm-review, add retired-word refusal branch, scrub bot-posted reply texts of CI trigger words."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","reason":"Update the inline comment naming the contributor trigger."},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py","reason":"Update the docstring naming the contributor trigger."},{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md","reason":"Contributor guide: instruct the new trigger word and contrast it with CI recheck."},{"path":"docs/review-policy.md","reason":"Coverage-gap remediation table and the contributor re-review section name the new word."},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"Reference to the self-service trigger renamed."},{"path":"docs/adr/0069-retryable-coverage-gap-bounded-deferral.md","reason":"Reference to the re-review trigger renamed."},{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","reason":"Contributor landing flow names the new trigger word."},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"Operator runbook names the new trigger word."},{"path":"infra/gerrit/webhooks.config","reason":"Comment naming the contributor trigger."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot_retrigger.py","reason":"Update existing matcher/near-miss tests to the new word; add retired-word refusal and ini-substring-safety tests."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot_retrigger_attestation_6a81.py","reason":"Update the attestation-path comment events to the new trigger word."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot.py","reason":"Update the comment referencing the contributor trigger."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e1aa-28c9-e9a2-45a6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a4ab0511-769e-41e2-aa32-5247505ff307","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["gerrit","ci","retrigger"],"ticket_id":"0d78-6c15-db26-4cea","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prevent recheck-review from retriggering CI","verify_commands":[{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"dispatch or reconciler\"","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"all four capability call sites isinstance-guarded"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_capability_guard_a3fa.py -q","dd_id":"AC2","dd_text":"absent capability = observable designed skip (log + count + bridge alert)"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_capability_guard_a3fa.py -q","dd_id":"AC3","dd_text":"present-but-raising keeps the existing failure signal, not conflated"},{"command":"make typecheck","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"casts survive; typecheck green"},{"command":"make lint","dd_id":"AC7","dd_text":"no src/rebar file exceeds the 800-LOC cap"},{"command":"grep -rl \"recheck-review\" tests/","dd_id":"AC5c","dd_text":"Retired word under tests/ only in the refusal-branch module"}]},"source_event_uuids":["106cbf47-4e76-4997-aae4-533e57bf0131","4bd228ca-c4f7-4bd3-ae62-70a30c13c1e9","0ee01cc7-fc2d-4fa2-8a63-0e6f43f9dd23","11af6ebe-6f4f-4be4-b8fc-3f2f66fd5be3","894acfd3-7f4c-4e1e-904a-d29abd360a50","5dfa5248-69bf-42b3-81db-84cfd69d8764","fa7c01fa-2742-4019-bcd5-903b9f3a0048","ef5f3e6f-1c88-4a2a-839c-5ae0ae870e34","4cffe5d6-a3ef-4ea1-bfb5-d9f9d50f00e1","10bd0023-95a6-4229-a10f-540acef8263f","f23023f3-a40f-46c1-b58a-4fe20aab4399","2c99d192-4387-41ff-977c-3cc1d53fed65","e5ecb898-f055-4c52-81c6-f92f1c198991","4f93bf74-47bc-4642-a27b-77e95c5c6fc8","06cdd94e-b53c-40c5-a138-b113961300d3","e443ad0f-5c7c-46fa-b9c4-d018b249725f","a4ab0511-769e-41e2-aa32-5247505ff307","5b4b5477-2b7a-4c96-9647-f7ea30471a76","0ab980c2-8228-4f6b-8f76-2a3859079e25"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786507308379804905,"uuid":"dc4f4f21-1dd2-4957-ad9b-c9f07f8b345a"}